    "title": "Pauli terms and the cubic coefficient",
    "full_tex": "Let $D=\\pi_0\\,i^{axy+bxz+cyz+dxyz}$ with $\\pi_0\\in\\{I,\\pi\\}$, $a,b,c\\in\\F_2$ and $d\\in\\Z/4$. (a) If $d$ is odd, then $D^\\dagger PD$ has at least eight Pauli terms for every non-diagonal three-qubit Pauli $P$. (b) If $d$ is even, then for every $p\\in\\F_2^3$ the labels $v$ with $DT_pP_vT_p^\\dagger D^\\dagger\\in\\C_2(3)$ form a subspace of dimension at least five.\n"
  },
  "finite_domain": "The 32 forms with d odd times the 56 non-diagonal Paulis; the 256 forms DT_p with d even times the 64 Pauli labels.",
